WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.776 --> 00:00:03.040
(film whirring)

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.140
- [Host] The Crown Season
3 kicks off in 1964,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.550
17 years after the start of Season 1.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.920
Now, that's a lot of history.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.150
The season ushers in a new era
of Beatles, silver jubilees

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.720
and moon landings.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.570
The Queen is now rapidly
approaching her 40s,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.430
Charles and Anne are coming of age

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.040
and Britain is a very different place.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.530
Whether you're after a refresh
or are brand new to The Crown

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:27.570
and want to jump straight
in, this video is for you.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.280
We're not recapping
everything that happens

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.930
in Season 1 and 2, just
the key parts of the story

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.100
that have a big impact on Season 3.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.570
Quick reminder, the timeline
of The Crown is factual,

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.770
but it is a drama.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.320
So while The Crown is
meticulously researched,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.730
some creative license is used

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.150
to drive the personal stories.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.330
Season 3 sees Elizabeth
contemplate the life

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.360
she could have had

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.990
if she'd never become queen.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.320
Because if you remember,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.673
she was never really
meant to wear the crown.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.360
Her uncle, Edward VIII, great
grandson of icon, legend

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.870
and star Queen Victoria
ascended the throne

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.680
after the death of his father.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.470
However, in a shock twist
only the British monarchs

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.950
know how to serve, Edward
abdicated that same year

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.110
because he wanted to marry

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.863
an American divorcee named Wallis Simpson.

00:01:12.737 --> 00:01:15.329
- [Royal] His love for her
has destroyed everything.

00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:16.170
- It is love.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.460
- [Host] You see, as the
King of the United Kingdom,

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.250
he was also Head of the Church

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.440
and marrying a divorcee
was out of the question.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.310
So he chose love and moved to France.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.710
There's a Madonna movie all
about it for those interested.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.230
But what does that mean for Elizabeth?

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.020
Now, with Edward gone,
his little brother Albert

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.570
who had lived in his
brother's shadow until now

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.233
stepped up to become King George VI.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:45.180
With a new king came a
new heir, enter Elizabeth.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.190
Okay, let's fast forward to 1947.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.420
Princess Elizabeth
marries Philip Mountbatten

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.030
in a super understated ceremony.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.710
In The Crown, we see Philip portrayed

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.200
as a very proud man.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.710
He struggles from the off when it comes

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:01.060
to joining the royal family
and being second to his wife.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.320
That's the dynamic he
continues to struggle with

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.660
throughout the show.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.660
Though, as he approaches
middle age in Season 3,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.980
we see his concerns shift
slightly as he comes to terms

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.020
with having lived a life of duty

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.713
rather than a life of passion.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.530
After marrying, Elizabeth and
Philip have four children,

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.577
Charles, Anne, Andrew and Edward.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.690
In 1952, King George VI dies

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.533
following a lung cancer diagnosis.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.740
Elizabeth, who remember
was never really meant

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.510
to become queen, does just that.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.810
At George's funeral, we see
his older brother return

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.710
to the UK, which caused quite the pickle.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:43.810
More than a year later

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.240
and it's time for Elizabeth
to be crowned queen.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.500
When we see this period in
The Crown, we see Philip

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.880
ask to be excused from bowing
to his wife at her coronation

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.040
and asks that his children
not lose the name Mountbatten.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.650
After some back and forths,

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.040
both answered with a big resounding...

00:02:59.040 --> 00:02:59.873
- No.

00:03:01.874 --> 00:03:04.010
- [Host] Now that we have our
queen, this is a good time

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.550
to remind you that she
had a younger sister,

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:10.100
a younger sister who lived
in her older sister's shadow.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.940
Sound familiar?

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.670
In Season 3, we see Margaret
step into the spotlight

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.500
very publicly and here
are some iconic limericks

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.840
along the way.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.762
- And that asshole in Buckingham Palace.

00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:21.595
(laughing)

00:03:21.595 --> 00:03:23.010
- [Host] But we're also
seeing a woman dealing

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.793
with marriage woes and
forever being second fiddle.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.810
Jumping back to the '40s
and '50s, Margaret was often

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.470
said to be the louder, more
rambunctious of the sisters.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.610
She's certainly a lot of fun in The Crown.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.210
And when she deputizes for the Queen

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.000
and goes totally off script...

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.040
- Our ambassador to the
United States of America,

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.740
Sir Roger Makins,

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.460
the only honest thing to
come out of Washington.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.300
- [Host] She causes a stir with people

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.410
including the Prime
Minister Winston Churchill

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.380
and the Queen herself.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.593
That defiance of protocol
continues in the new season.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.650
In 1953, Margaret became
involved with Peter Townsend

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.970
a former RAF Officer and
later Queen's Equerry.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.855
The public loved their relationship.

00:04:03.855 --> 00:04:05.326
- [Reporter] Pressmen and sightseers

00:04:05.326 --> 00:04:07.244
hoping for a glimpse of the couple.

00:04:07.244 --> 00:04:09.270
- [Host] But Townsend is a divorcee,

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.510
which as we've learned is less than ideal.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.790
Long story short, the Church, Parliament

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.070
and other senior royals do
not approve of the union.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:22.162
Townsend is sent away and
ultimately the relationship ends.

00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:25.670
(classical music)

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.970
Despite promising to never love again,

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.650
Margaret eventually pairs
up with a fairly nice,

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.060
fairly boring man named Billy Wallace,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.583
but eventually breaks it off.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.690
In a very Love Island move,

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.460
Margaret then picks a
sexy bad boy photographer

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.433
named Antony Armstrong Jones.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.440
We see it all go down in Season 2

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.560
when he was taking
official portraits of her

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.660
and true to form, she went loge

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.020
and sent a seemingly
naked photo of herself

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.730
to the UK tabloids.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.230
- [Reader] And she's naked.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.630
- [Host] A lot of hoo-ha
later and eventually in 1960,

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.870
the two got married and went
on to have two children.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:03.790
Keep an eye on that particular union.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:07.043
It's a big and messy
plot point in Season 3.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.580
There are a couple of really
incredible episodes in Season 3

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.750
that focus on Prince Charles
and his coming of age.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.990
In Season 2, we saw his father struggle

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.020
with a seemingly sensitive child.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.210
- So we're not just becoming

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.170
a wet mandy-pandy monarchy twit.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.250
- [Host] Philip believed his
own upbringing made him tough.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:29.050
So the same needed to be
true of his eldest son.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.270
We saw Charles struggle when
his father insisted he attend

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.560
Gordonstoun School and the two continue

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.110
to have a troubled relationship

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.147
now that Charles is growing up.

00:05:38.147 --> 00:05:40.140
(light music)

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.110
Back to the Queen for a sec,
our story has seen some ups

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.864
and downs in her marriage over the years.

00:05:45.864 --> 00:05:47.940
- Philip, don't you get ever back here!

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.960
- [Host] The power dynamic
with Philip is a key thing

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.280
to keep in your mind and
we've watched it play out

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.290
across many episodes.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.290
The two are arguably
more settled in Season 3.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.680
And we see some real moments of love.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.350
But there's no denying
Philip is a complex character

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.310
with a lot of baggage.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.830
The other thing to note
is the way her stoicism

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.140
is portrayed in the show.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.500
When she met Jackie Kennedy in
Season 2, we saw her ability

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.140
to deal with bad behavior
in a proper fashion.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.890
Where others might have
screamed and shouted...

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.680
- I'm quite sure that you
meant no harm nor disrespect.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.520
After all, why would you?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.170
- [Host] In Season 3, we
see key moments in her life

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:27.000
when you may expect a
more emotional response

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.020
but after years of being on the throne,

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.600
she's learned as Margaret put it...

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:32.780
- Camera perfect.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.210
- [Host] That's pretty
much you need to know

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.040
about our story thus far.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.120
There are a few other things
you should probably know

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.740
about the UK in the 1960s,

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.680
one of which is the swing
to liberal politics.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.620
The Conservative Party had
been hit by a sex scandal,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.000
the Profumo Affair for those interested.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.590
And that as well as a
growing liberal movement

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.680
across the country led to a small

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.063
Labor majority win in 1964.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.840
We see some of the ups and downs

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.310
of the politics in Season 3.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.350
So we won't show a load of spoilers,

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.380
but with the growing liberal
movement came a renewed sense

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.000
of anti-monarchy sentiment
across the nation.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.680
It's fascinating to see how
it plays out in Season 3.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.730
- They want our heads on stakes.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:13.660
- [Host] One more thing

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.760
and then we'll leave you to it, miners.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.640
The struggle of the miners
in 1960s and '70s Britain

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.490
is well documented.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.150
We had a national coal board
trying to keep costs down

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.120
and a national union of mine workers

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.110
who wanted increased
wages, fairer working hours

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.810
and a change to safety
conditions, among other things.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.553
The two got into many
disputes over the years.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.233
In Season 3, we'll see our monarchy react.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.670
Finally, meet our cast.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:44.770
We're 17 years ahead by now
and everybody is a bit older.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.830
In fact, the Queen herself is in her 50s

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.033
by the end of Season 3.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.270
Olivia Colman is wearing the
crown as Queen Elizabeth II,

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:54.570
Helena Bonham Carter is playing Margaret,

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.560
and we have Tobias
Menzies as Prince Philip.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.960
Ben Daniels plays Tony Armstrong
Jones, Margaret's husband.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.380
Charles Dance is Lord
Mountbatten, Philip's uncle.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.490
Marion Bailey is the Queen Mother,

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.390
while Josh O'Connor and Erin Doherty

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:11.023
play Prince Charles and
Princess Anne respectively.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.830
Okay, we're done.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.050
You're all caught up.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.600
Watch The Crown now streaming on Netflix.

